'' WITHOUT '-exx' THERE IS NO NAMING, which is the half a test of the feature alone
'' would not catch: emitting the pair unconditionally would pass every assertion in
'' errfuncname.test and put two runtime calls in the prologue of every procedure ever
'' compiled. Measured: fbc emits none of this for '-e', for '-ex' or for no flag at all.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -ex --emit-ir tests/codegen/src/errfuncname.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-NOT: fb_ErrorSetFuncName
'' EXPECT-NOT: fb_ErrorSetModName
